                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "So ... I've played this game for a bit over 9 hours and just made it through my first way.\nIn general I've waited for this game quite some time since Texic announced he was making one.\n\nOverall this game is great. Fitting music (even though sometimes the sudden changes made it feel weird), awesome drawings, hours and hours of gameplay.\nIn the english version there are quite some typing mistakes which sometimes are really annoying, but most of the translation is fine.\nOften i laughed, followed by the feeling I had a connection to the situation (like i had something like this before), sometimes the story made me sad, but not for too long (except for the ending, but i will get to that)\nYou have a lot of choices to make, but at some times there are too many choices, at others there are no choices when it would have been nice to decide yourself what to say or do, not the character.\nOverall i do recommend this game, even though i am not 100% happy.\n\nTo be fair, this is my first visual novel, I do not have any other experience with this genre, so the following point is just my subjective opinion:\nIn my playthrough i often had the feeling that nothing i did influenced the way the story is going. Around half the time I had my eyes set on one target and did what was (in my opinion) the right way to get there. But in the end i got something that felt wrong. It felt like I've wasted several hours to get an ending which did not make me happy that I've played the game.  It gave me the feeling of failiure. About half an hour before the ending I was like \"okay, this is going into the right direction\" and then suddenly all came down to what i hope is the saddest ending (because it totally differed from the usual tone of the comics and i don't want there to be an even sadder ending). I was waiting and really begging for a twist, for something to make the ending \"better\", to give me the feeling of happines i expected. But then the credits rolled and i was shocked. The game did a 180° turn in like 5 minutes and even the pretty minor glance of a \"happy ending\" did not change the feeling that I had no real chance to end this the way i wanted. This ending felt completely wrong and made me sad. Not in a positive way, just straight up sad. And that is nothing a game should do, even a graphic novel.",
